<p>There is an adjustment period. Not because the shoe is flawed — because your foot muscles have been carried by cushioning for years and have to take that work back gradually. An hour or two a day in the first week, then longer. Even the maker's five-star reviews mention a learning curve, and the customers who love these most are the ones who eased in. Build up over a week or two and you give them the best possible run.</p>

